    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Namespaces by reserved-but-unused CPU",
      "description": "Reserved is what the workload asked Kubernetes to set aside; used is the 95th percentile of what it actually consumed over the window. The gap is capacity nobody can schedule on. CI namespaces burst by design and kube-system is platform overhead \u2014 neither is waste in the same sense.\n\nFull explanation: apps/platform-capacity/dashboard.md in the ovh-cluster repo.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "datasource": {
