    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Resources with no requests",
      "description": "A namespace here declares no request for one resource or the other, so the scheduler treats that resource as free and packs nodes past what they can hold. When a node then runs short the kubelet evicts whatever is handiest, which is rarely the workload at fault. Two incidents on this cluster started this way, both taking the storage driver down with them. These namespaces need requests set, not lowered.\n\nFull explanation: apps/platform-capacity/dashboard.md in the ovh-cluster repo.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "capacity-pg"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 2,
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "cpu_p95_cores"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "CPU used (p95)"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.width",
                "value": 140
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "mem_max_gb"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "Mem peak (GiB)"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.width",
                "value": 140
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true,
        "cellHeight": "sm",
        "footer": {
          "show": false,
          "reducer": [
            "sum"
          ],
          "fields": ""
        },
        "sortBy": [
          {
            "displayName": "Mem peak (GiB)",
            "desc": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "capacity-pg"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "format": "table",
          "rawSql": "SELECT namespace, cpu_p95_cores, mem_max_gb FROM namespace_trend WHERE taken_at = (SELECT max(taken_at) FROM namespace_trend) AND (cpu_req_cores < 0.05 OR mem_req_gb < 0.05) AND (cpu_p95_cores > 0.1 OR mem_max_gb > 0.1) ORDER BY mem_max_gb DESC LIMIT 20"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Namespaces by reserved-but-unused memory",
      "description": "The memory equivalent: reserved minus the highest the namespace ever reached during the window. A negative value is the opposite problem \u2014 it used more than it reserved, which is what causes evictions rather than cost, and is why the list is worth reading from both ends.\n\nFull explanation: apps/platform-capacity/dashboard.md in the ovh-cluster repo.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13
      },
      "datasource": {
